## LangWatch SDK 2.0 separates dashboard calls from analytics reports

Source: LangWatch — https://github.com/langwatch/langwatch/releases/tag/typescript-sdk%40v2.0.0
Published: 2026-10-28
Channel: github

LangWatch is a platform for observing and evaluating AI applications. Its TypeScript SDK 2.0.0 release changes the meaning of a familiar API path: client.dashboards now addresses the new Dashboards product rather than the older Reports API. Existing report operations move to client.analyticsReports. The release also renames Reports tools exposed through Model Context Protocol, the interface agents use to call external tools.

For illustration, a team might have a script that retrieves a recurring agent-quality report. After upgrading, continuing to call the dashboards path would target a different product. The useful migration check is whether the script still retrieves the intended report, not simply whether its request succeeds. This example illustrates the compatibility risk; the notes do not report a measured customer incident.

The release adds REST creation and deletion for dashboard boards and records each request’s credential type. Legacy project keys become ingestion-only. Those changes make both API paths and permissions relevant to upgrade testing. This is a major SDK release with explicit breaking changes, so teams should review report consumers and credentials together before rolling it through production monitoring workflows.

Why it matters: For LangWatch integration owners: inventory dashboards calls, migrate report consumers to analyticsReports, and verify read permissions separately from telemetry ingestion.

