## Phoenix preserves custom evaluator metadata alongside results

Source: Arize AI / Phoenix — https://github.com/Arize-ai/phoenix/releases/tag/%40arizeai/phoenix-evals%402.7.1
Published: 2026-10-28
Channel: github

Phoenix provides tools for inspecting AI runs and scoring their results. Its TypeScript evaluation package 2.7.1 fixes createEvaluator, a helper that wraps custom evaluation functions, so it retains metadata those functions return. For illustration, a team’s scorer could attach context explaining a result; preserving that context helps a reviewer interpret the score. The release establishes metadata preservation, not improved scoring accuracy or any particular metadata format. It lists this as a narrow patch and reports no benchmark or broader evaluator redesign.

Why it matters: For custom evaluator authors: run a known example through createEvaluator and confirm its returned metadata reaches the result you inspect.

