## Phoenix keeps schema descriptions and defaults when converting prompts

Source: Arize AI / Phoenix — https://github.com/Arize-ai/phoenix/releases/tag/%40arizeai/phoenix-client%407.16.3
Published: 2026-10-28
Channel: github

Phoenix’s client helps applications work with AI prompts and their structured definitions. Version 7.16.3 fixes toSDK conversion of prompt tool and response-format schemas: description, default and other keywords next to anyOf are retained. The anyOf keyword describes alternative valid shapes. For illustration, a test prompt using alternatives and an adjacent description should keep both when converted for use. This patch concerns the definition passed onward; it does not establish that a model follows that definition. The release supplies no measured evaluation improvement.

Why it matters: For teams testing structured prompts: compare converted schemas with the originals, including annotations beside anyOf, before attributing changed outputs to a model.

